x86_64-windows  Refused before it reaches the question it asks: a class-typed throw needs the Microsoft ThrowInfo chain pointed at a class - a type descriptor and a catchable type per class, and a _CTA array listing the thrown class and its bases - and cxx1 emits those four objects for a fundamental type only. throw-class.notarget records that lag at length. The question itself is Itanium's alone: there is no `__cxa_end_catch` on that ABI, a handler being a funclet the runtime ends the catch for when it returns, so nothing here has a counterpart to get wrong. handler-exit-end-catch.notarget says the same about the jumps.
